Your example is not correct, because Next uses a new version of JSX transformer since 9.5.3 and You should use `@emotion/babel-plugin` instead of `@emotion/babel-preset-css-prop`. @emotion/babel-preset-css-prop works only with `classic` JSX runtime which is not set as default.

Also, to use new JSX runtimes You need to configure your custom babel config.
```javascript
{
  "presets": [
    [
      "next/babel",
      {
        "preset-react": {
          "runtime": "automatic",
          "importSource": "@emotion/react"
        }
      }
    ]
  ],
  "plugins": ["@emotion/babel-plugin"]
}
``` 

Check: 
- https://emotion.sh/docs/babel
- https://reactjs.org/blog/2020/09/22/introducing-the-new-jsx-transform.html

